Absolutely. ClipGenius is much bigger than an “AI clip cutter.” What you're describing is closer to an AI video post-production + content repurposing platform.

The important part is that we should architect it around the user's intent/prompt, rather than around a fixed list of editing buttons.

The core ClipGenius concept

The workflow becomes:

Raw Video → User Prompt → AI understands the content → AI edits → AI creates platform-specific content → Publish

For example, a user uploads a 45-minute sermon and says:

“Turn this into engaging Christian content. Remove pauses and repetitions, add dynamic captions, emphasize powerful statements, use relevant images/B-roll where appropriate, and make the clips suitable for Instagram, TikTok and YouTube Shorts.”

ClipGenius should ideally handle the whole pipeline.

