1. I would structure ClipGenius into 5 engines
Engine 1 — Content Understanding

This is the brain.

When the video is uploaded, ClipGenius should first:

Transcribe the entire video
Identify speakers
Detect topics
Detect key statements
Detect emotional/high-energy moments
Identify questions and answers
Detect stories
Detect calls-to-action
Detect silence/pauses
Detect repetition
Detect potentially viral moments
Analyze visual scenes
Understand the user's prompt

So instead of blindly cutting every 30 seconds, ClipGenius understands:

“What is actually happening in this video?”

That becomes your competitive advantage.

2. AI Editing Engine

Then the AI creates an Edit Decision List (EDL).

For example:

00:00–00:07 → Remove intro silence
00:07–00:19 → Keep
00:19–00:24 → Remove repetition
00:24–01:15 → Keep
01:15–01:21 → Add punch-in
01:21–01:30 → Add B-roll
01:30–01:34 → Emphasize phrase

The user shouldn't necessarily need to understand any of this.

They just say:

“Make it fast-paced and engaging.”

ClipGenius translates that into editing instructions.

